      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-03-13_WidnesExaminer_art0011" n="art0011">
        <head>BILLIARDS.</head>
        <p>BILLIARDS.</p>
        <p>TLIE CHA.34PIONSHIP OF WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>Oa Friday evening a billiard match for the amateur championship of Warrington (500 up) was played in the Church of the Sacred Heart Catholic Association rooms, the contestants being Mr. Drinkwater, of Padgate-lane, and Mr. Connor, of Bank Quay. Mr. Connor, who ran out an easy winner by no fewer than 234 points, made 'roast breaks of 22, 21, 24, 86, and 37.</p>
      </div>
