      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-03-13_WidnesExaminer_art0018" n="art0018">
        <p>WOOL WICH ELECTION.—Mr. Will Crooks, the Labou candidate, won a notable victory over his Unionis opponent. Mr. Geoffrey Drage, at Woolwich, on Wednesday, the figures being:—Crooks (L.), 8,687 ; Drage (U.), 5,458. Labour majority, 4,229. Following the decision of Mr. Justice Buckley in the London and Globe case a summons against Mr. Whitaker Wrightwas applied for and granted by the magistrate at the London Guildhall, to be heard on the 19th inst. On Wednesday morning, however, it was discovered that Mr. Wright left the country some time ago. Dur- ing tan day, therefore, a, warrant was obtained for his arrest. He is understood to be in Egypt.</p>
      </div>
