        <p>PRUDENTIAL ASSURANCE COMPANY, LIMITED. CHIEF OFFICR HOLBORN BAR, LONDON. Summary of the Report presented at the Fifty-fourth Annual Meeting, held on bth March 1903. ORDINARY BRANCH.—The number of Policies issued during the year was 69,662, assuring the sum of £6,680,C50, and producing a New Annual Premium Inaome of £364,068. The Premiums received during the year were £3,01,458, being an increase of £161,503 over the year 1901. The Claims of the year amaunted to £1,296,693. The number of Deaths was 6,895, and 3,952 Endowment Assur- ances matured. The number of Polieles in force at the end of the year was 680,631. INDUSTRIAL BRANCH —The Premiums receivel during the year were £5,690,907, being an increase of £161,446, The Claims of the year amounted to £2,140,645. The number of Deaths was 212,701, and 3,369 Endowment Assurances matured. The number of Free Polcies granted during the year to those Policy-holders of five years' standing who desired to discontinue their payments was 84,060, the number in force being 836,884. The number of Free Policies which became Claims during the year was 19.170. The total number of Policies in force at the end of the year was 14.770.865; their average duration is ten years. The Assets of the Company, in both branches, as shown in the Balance Sheet, are £47,155,201, being an increase of £3,163,175 ever those of 1931. The :staff Provident Fund, which was founded in 1898 for the benefit of the outdoor staff, shows a satisfactory increase for the year, the total amount sten iing to the credit of the Fund being £115,608. GENERAL BALANCE SHEET OF THE PRUDENTIAL ASSURANCE COMPANY, LIMITED, ON THE 31ST DECEMBER, 1932. LIABILITIES. 2 8. d. Shareholders' Capital .. . Ordinary Branch Funds Industrial Branch Fund Reserve Fund . 1,050,060 0 0 Investments Reserve Fund 400.000 0 0 Claims under life policies admitted 111,843 7 3 £47,155,201 6 8 ASSETS. £ a. d. British Government securities ......... 3.556,324 I 9 Indian and colonial government seeurities 4,708,709 14 7 Railway and other debentures and deben- ture stocks 3,607,84 4 9 Loans on County Council, Municipal and other rates Freehold ground rents and Scotch ten duties 3.421,786 15 8 Freehold and leasehold property Mortgages on property within the United Kingdom Railway, Gas, and Water stocks 6,306,488 6 7 Suez Can.l Shares Telegraph and other shares 88 889 15 3 Metropolitan Consolidated stock, and City of London bonds 279.108 11 11 Bank of England stock 200,559 18 6 Colonial and Foreign corporation stocks Foreign government securities Reversions and Life Interests 1,007,412 15 0 Loans on the Company's Policies Rent charges 247.909 4 2 Outstanding premiums and agents' balances 469.059 11 0 Outstanding interest and rents Cash—ln hands of superintendents. Ditto—On current accounts, and in hand 173,651 6 4 £47.155.201 6 0 EDGAR HORNE, Chairman. HENRY H ARBRN, }Directors. J. W. SIMMONS, THOS. O. DEWEY, IJolnt General WILLIAM HUGHES, f Managers. FREDBITICK SCI4OOLING, Actuary. D. W. STABLE, Secretary. SUPERINTENDENT : Mr. U. II ICH OLLS, 76. ALBERT ROAD, WIDNES. We have examined the Cash transactions (receipts and payments) affecting the accounts of the Assets and Invest- ments for the year ended December 31st, 19C2, and we find the same in good order and properly von.thed. We have Also examined the Deeds and Securities, Certificates, &amp;c., representing the Assets and Investments set out in the above accounts, and we certify that they were in possession and safe custody as on December 31st, 19C2. DELOITTE, DRYER, GRIFFITHS, &amp; Co., Chartered Accountants. 18th February, 1903.</p>
