        <p>----- - - - TO MAKE A HOUSZ A REAL HOME FURNISH IT AT P'TTS'S LONDON-ROA D, M ANC RESTER, (Just past Station through Railway Arch.) ALSO AT PITTS'S PANTHEON, GAYTHORN, (Just past Manchester Central Station), PATRONISED BY ROYALTY, NOBILITY, Bcc. WHAT'S IN A NAME? That which we term a rose, if called by any other name would smell as sweet." Young and unsophisHeated as she was, Juliet, nevertheless, voiced a truism when she so expressed herself. Still, despite this, there is very considerable value, both sentimental and financial in a good name, especially in these keen competitive and not, we regret to say, over- scrupulous times. Nowadays a good name is more precious than rubies—in fact, some firms would not part with theirs for all the wealth in the world. A good name is not only a source of pride to its possessor, but a safeguard to the public. Take, for instance, the name of PITTS'S which for many years has been familia, in your months as a household word. This name to connection with an article hallmarks it as thoroughly reliable, durable, tasteful, and the BEST VALUE obtainable. Everyone of experience is aware of this. hecce the ever-increasing volume of business flowing to PITTIs'S of LONDON ROAD and GAYTHORN. PITTS'S PEERLESS HOUSES OF FURNI- TURE at 15i, 22.1, 28i, 381, 50. 75, 100, 200. up to 1,000 guineas, have been pronounced by practical people the PINNACLE OF PERFECTION. Their high artistic and Intrinsic merits, their beauty and valise, are apparent to casual inspection, which sloser examination and wear only confirm. Full particulars and NEW ILLUSTRATED FURNISHING GUIDE. containing 807 designs price 50 per cent. below elsewhere, post free. Cash prices only quoted. Deferred payments 10 per cent. extra. PITTS'S DISPLAY OF BARGAINS is cer- thinly unequalled in the provinces. The following are a fair sample all in really excellent condition HALL FURNITURE,consists of Mahogany Hat stand,two Chairs, Side Tables, Linolaum, two Wool Rugs, three Cooo